layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /order-online/
pageKey: orderOnline
title: "Order Tajima Ramen Online | Pickup and Delivery"
description: "Order Tajima Ramen online for pickup or delivery. One link per San Diego location, plus Kihei on Maui."
---
{#
  /order-online/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.

  Third-biggest page on the site: 5,648 clicks, 355,269 impressions.
  Transactional intent. The brief's whole section plan is four words long:
  "One card per location. Name, neighborhood, Toast link. Nothing else. This
  page's only job is not to be in the way." So there is no hero video, no
  story, no noodle band. Cards and out.

  THE ORDERING URLS ARE UNVERIFIED AND THIS IS THE BIGGEST OPEN RISK ON THE
  PAGE. They came from the design concept, not from Tajima. CLIENT_FACTS.md
  lists per-location ordering URLs as CONFIRM. SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md flags three
  specific problems and all three are still present, recorded per location in
  locations.json under orderUrlNote:

    - Two competing URL patterns. Convoy, Mercury, and East Village use
      /v2/online-order. College Heights uses /v3. The brief says pick one and
      verify all seven resolve. Neither has happened.
    - Crown Point's Toast slug reads `tajima-pacific-beach-3782-ingraham-street`.
      Left exactly as found. The brief says flag it, do not silently fix it,
      because the slug may be what Toast actually uses and editing it breaks
      the cart.
    - Plaza Bonita is a `toasttakeout.page.link` shortlink rather than a
      toasttab.com URL.

  Maui has no ordering URL at all. Its card renders without an order button
  rather than inventing one.

  A dead ordering link on this page costs more than a missing one. Click-test
  all seven before launch.
#}

<section class="order-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="order-hero__inner">
    <h1 class="order-hero__title" id="page-title">Order Online</h1>
    <p class="order-hero__sub">
      Pick the room you want it from. Pickup and delivery, straight through to that kitchen's order page. <a href="/menu/">See the menu</a> first if you want.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="order-grid" aria-label="Order by location">
  <div class="order-grid__inner">
    {%- for loc in locations.items %}
    {#
      The id is the anchor target for /order-online/#<slug>, which is where the
      Locations mega menu's per-location "Order online" buttons point. Those do
      NOT link straight to Toast: every ordering URL is still unverified
      (two competing URL patterns, Crown Point's slug reading
      tajima-pacific-beach, Plaza Bonita on a page.link shortlink). Routing
      through this page means one place to fix when the click-test happens,
      instead of seven links scattered through the nav.
    #}
    <article class="order-card" id="{{ loc.id }}">
      <div>
        <h2 class="order-card__name">{{ loc.name }}</h2>
        {#- Dedupe: Plaza Bonita and Maui have neighborhood == locality, which
            printed "National City, National City". Same guard the home router uses. -#}
        <p class="order-card__hood">
          {%- if loc.neighborhood and loc.neighborhood != loc.address.locality -%}
            {{ loc.neighborhood }}, {{ loc.address.locality }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
      </div>

      {%- if loc.orderUrl %}
      <a class="order-card__cta" href="{{ loc.orderUrl }}" rel="noopener">
        Order from {{ loc.name }}
        <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span>
      </a>
      {%- else %}
      {# No ordering URL on record. Offer the phone, which is confirmed, rather
         than a button that goes nowhere. #}
      <a class="order-card__cta order-card__cta--quiet" href="tel:+1-{{ loc.phone | replace('(', '') | replace(') ', '-') | replace(' ', '-') }}">
        Call {{ loc.phone }}
      </a>
      {%- endif %}
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="loc-close" aria-labelledby="close-title">
  <div class="loc-close__inner">
    <h2 class="loc-close__title" id="close-title">Not sure which room?</h2>
    <p class="loc-close__sub">
      <a href="/locations/">All six San Diego rooms</a>, with addresses and phone numbers.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
